From eae76cc8eaa0bc3b72d274da6526a0168ba58401 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:21:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Version pill update poll: passive, keeps state on
 error, drain clock

Review of the first commit (subagent, REQUEST_CHANGES), addressed:
- The 10 s progress poll is passive with no `foreground` priority: it never
  cold-starts a local backend and never counts as user activity, so it can't
  open the sleep gate (electron/power-settle.ts).
- An unreachable host (most often: restarting for this very update) keeps
  the pill's last state; only an answered "nothing in progress" ends an
  update and refreshes the version. One request per host at a time; a
  connection switch clears the old remote's state.
- The bar rides the icon slot with the button `relative`: the label sits in
  a truncating (overflow-hidden) span that clipped it.
- The bar fills on the drain pass's own clock (new state_elapsed_s), which
  the drainer's cap is measured on; the tooltip still counts from due.
- session_auto_continue logs when a held message cannot be journaled
  because a sibling's live turn holds the marker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
